# Angular templates

When editing files matching this rule.

## Scope

- Applies to: `**/*.component.html`

## Conventions

- Always use separate `.html` files in Angular components; do not use inline templates.
- Use semantic HTML with proper accessibility attributes.
- Apply Tailwind classes consistently with the project's configured prefix, if one exists.
- When styling text elements inside Material layout components, add a `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>`, `<h4>`, `<h5>`, `<h6>`, `<span>`, or `<p>` element as appropriate and then style the element with Tailwind classes to avoid getting overridden by Material styles.
- Use Angular control flow (`@if`, `@for`) instead of structural directives.
- If a signal is used in the template multiple times, use the `@let` syntax to declare the variable at the top of the template and then use it multiple times.
